  "description": "SAXHIJ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H144 O10 Pr8 Se18,5.25(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 1 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 2 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 2 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 2 O neighbors; Pr1B (Pr) has 1 O neighbors; Pr2B (Pr) has 2 O neighbors; Pr3B (Pr) has 2 O neighbors; Pr4B (Pr) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.847-3.924 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 117.18-124.24°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C128H144O10Pr8Se18·5.25(C4H8O).",
